{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion (RNA + image) provides a meaningful accuracy gain over single-modality approaches, and which encoder pairings are viable. config_004 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) directly tests this core hypothesis with a balanced, moderate-cost setup: scvi_n200 captures learned biological structure in the RNA space (more informative than PCA for downstream fusion), resnet50 is a well-established and relatively cheap image backbone, singleprofile keeps training cost low, and concat is the simplest fusion strategy to establish a baseline. This experiment will (1) confirm whether the multimodal pipeline yields a usable accuracy signal, (2) provide a reference point to later compare against RNA-only or image-only baselines, and (3) inform whether upgrading to multiprofile, transformer aggregation, or ViT-L is worthwhile in subsequent experiments. Expected relative cost: moderate — lower than multiprofile + transformer + ViT-L configurations but higher than PCA + resnet50 singleprofile setups, making it an efficient first probe of the search space."
}

